<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Havran Cold-War border hike — Stará Knížecí Huť–Huťský rybník–Zlatý Potok–Havran out-and-back [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Stará Knížecí Huť, walk through Huťský rybník and Zlatý Potok to Havran’s former Cold War surveillance site, then retrace the route, about 15.3 km in total. Forest roads and paths lead to a steep concrete-panel ascent. Green and blue markings cover parts of the route; continuous yellow marking between the pond and Zlatý Potok is not confirmed. The Celní potok ford must be safe, and no reliable bridge or planks are established. Choose dry, snow- and ice-free daylight, with sturdy footwear and supplies. Climbing the exposed tower stairs is optional and depends on access and weather. Postpone if any required crossing or passage is unsafe or closed, and respect forest restrictions and forestry work. Walking time and height-gain figures are approximate; allow extra time for crossing checks, the steep ascent and stops.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Two-dimensional planning geometry; not navigation-grade.

